IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sarca-licensing`

-- Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA), with the Regulations 1997 -- the Q&A layer: the questions
-- people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question
-- form drops the questions that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the security officer or licence applicant -- the baseline's seat (Jake, k060), whose 31 questions are asked here
--     by calling the baseline's functions in sarca-licensing.l4;
--   * a business that supplies security officers to others, a security agent (s 11) -- bound by s 15 (its own
--     licence, held for a company under s 43), s 20 (no unlicensed officer employed), s 21 (no advertising without the
--     licence), and the employer whom s 19 requires a licensed officer to work for;
--   * a person who hires or employs security for their own property -- who meets s 12(2) (an in-house guard), s 20 (if
--     the guard needs a licence) and s 15 (the firm hired must be licensed).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The licensing
-- officer, the Commissioner, the State Administrative Tribunal and the courts are never seats: what they may or must do
-- appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * `I hold a security officer's licence` (BOOLEAN; the officer): FALSE settles the questions the Act asks only of a
--     licensee -- s 19 working terms, batons and firearms, renewing (ss 49(3), 55), the shift conditions, the identity
--     card, the reports of ss 77 and 77A, s 67A and drug testing. TRUE settles the one question about the time before the
--     licence is issued (s 20, from the officer's seat);
--   * `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence` (BOOLEAN; the officer): FALSE settles the three questions
--     about one past matter (ss 4A, 4B, reg 25). "Am I a prohibited person on this day", over all matters, arises for
--     every applicant and takes none;
--   * `the licensing officer refused to issue me a licence` and `the licensing officer refused to renew my licence`
--     (BOOLEAN; the officer): the times for the written reasons, s 57(1) and (2);
--   * `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` (BOOLEAN; the officer and the security business): FALSE
--     settles the penalty questions;
--   * `how I get security for my property` (`How I get security for my property`; the client): employing one's own guard
--     opens the s 12(2) and s 20 questions, hiring a firm the s 15 question, and both opens both. The two helpers that
--     read it list every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (what my work is, the issue test, the fees, the term, review)
-- takes no situation input.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's records (`My work`, `My past matter`,
-- `My application`) are taken as the baseline takes them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I work, or want to work, as a security officer`
    `I run a business that supplies security officers to others`
    `I hire or employ security for my own property`

DECLARE `How I get security for my property` IS ONE OF
    `I employ my own guard`
    `I hire a security firm to supply guards`
    `I do both`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years of disqualification` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `disqualified for` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER

-- The officer's answers that are the baseline's own enumerations, carried with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Training course, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Training course`

DECLARE `Licence decision, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Licence decision`

DECLARE `Licence term, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Licence term`

DECLARE `Renewal decision, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Renewal decision`

DECLARE `Notice duty, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Notice duty`

DECLARE `What happens to my licence, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `What happens to my licence`

-- The offences of a security business (s 15, s 20, s 21); the client's s 20 offence is the second.
DECLARE `My business's offence` IS ONE OF
    `supplying security officers without a security agent's licence (s 15)`
    `employing an unlicensed person as a security officer (s 20)`
    `advertising that I supply security officers without a security agent's licence (s 21)`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The client's situation (D8). Both list every value with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I employ my own guard, in` `how I get security for my property` IF
    CONSIDER `how I get security for my property`
    WHEN `I employ my own guard` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I hire a security firm to supply guards` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `I do both` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I hire a security firm, in` `how I get security for my property` IF
    CONSIDER `how I get security for my property`
    WHEN `I employ my own guard` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `I hire a security firm to supply guards` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I do both` THEN TRUE

-- The work of a guard the client employs directly, as the baseline's `My work` record, so that the baseline's s 12 test
-- (`Am I a security officer`) decides whether the guard is a security officer. The guard is paid and guards the
-- client's property; "my one employer, not a security agent" holds when the client is the guard's only employer (the
-- client role is for a person who is not a security agent); nothing else in the record bears on s 12.
GIVEN `works only for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `armed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My work`
`the work of my own guard` MEANS
    `My work` WITH
        `I am paid for it` IS TRUE
        `I watch, guard or protect property` IS TRUE
        `my one employer, not a security agent, employs me to guard its own property` IS `works only for me`
        `I carry a firearm or baton while working` IS `armed`
        `I escort a person as a guard or protector` IS FALSE
        `I advise on watching, guarding or protecting property` IS FALSE
        `I install, maintain or repair security equipment listed in s 14` IS FALSE
        `the equipment is in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft` IS FALSE
        `as a regular duty I control, screen or remove people at a venue or event` IS FALSE
        `I investigate people's conduct or character, or look for missing persons` IS FALSE
        `I supply other people to do security work` IS FALSE
        `I am on official duty as a police officer or in the Defence Force` IS FALSE
        `I am on official duty as a public officer` IS FALSE
        `I am a court security, custodial or prison services contract worker doing that work` IS FALSE
        `I hold a temporary licence covering this work` IS FALSE

-- ss 15, 20, 21: "Penalty: a fine of $15 000." Regulations Sch 5 Div 1 items 1 (s 15), 7 (s 20(1) or (2)) and 8
-- (s 21(1)): modified penalty $500 each.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My business's offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a court can fine for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supplying security officers without a security agent's licence (s 15)` THEN 15000
    WHEN `employing an unlicensed person as a security officer (s 20)` THEN 15000
    WHEN `advertising that I supply security officers without a security agent's licence (s 21)` THEN 15000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My business's offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the modified penalty for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supplying security officers without a security agent's licence (s 15)` THEN 500
    WHEN `employing an unlicensed person as a security officer (s 20)` THEN 500
    WHEN `advertising that I supply security officers without a security agent's licence (s 21)` THEN 500

§§ `For the security officer or licence applicant (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (sarca-licensing.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 3, 5, 11-20, 43 -- what my work is, and may I do it`

@export Does my work make me a security officer (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my work make me a security officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a security officer` `my work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the work I do need this licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) Part 3, 4 or 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the licence` IS A `Licence type` @desc The licence you are asking about
      `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the work I do need this licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`Does my work need this licence` `the licence` `my work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I excused from holding a licence for this work (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 5, s 42A; Regulations regs 5A, 5B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I excused from holding a licence for this work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`Am I excused from holding a licence` `my work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I do this work without holding a security officer's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I do this work without holding a security officer's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`May I do this work without a security officer's licence` `my work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I work as a licensed security officer on these terms (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `I am an employee, under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work under a contract of service or an apprenticeship, rather than as a contractor
      `the business I work for supplies the services of security officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business you work for supplies security officers to others (a security agent)
      `I am myself a licensed security agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security agent's licence yourself
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I work as a licensed security officer on these terms` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` `I hold a security officer's licence` `I am an employee, under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `the business I work for supplies the services of security officers` `I am myself a licensed security agent`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the business I work for be licensed as a security agent (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 11, 15, 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the business supplies the services of security officers to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business places security officers at clients' premises or otherwise supplies their services
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the business I work for be licensed as a security agent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence` `the business supplies the services of security officers to others`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The question is about the time before the licence is issued, so it arises only while I hold none: holding one
-- settles it to `does not arise for you`. Before then the answer is the baseline's, on FALSE: no.
@export May I be employed as a security officer before my licence is issued (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be employed as a security officer before my licence is issued` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be employed as a security officer` `I hold a security officer's licence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23-26 -- firearms and batons`

@export May I carry a baton at work (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 26; Regulations Sch 1 cl 9(2), 11(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `my licence has a baton endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your security officer's licence is endorsed under s 26
      `the baton is a type the Commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the baton is of a type approved by Gazette order
      `my baton training is within the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you completed approved baton training within 12 months of the last course
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I carry a baton at work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I carry a baton while working` `my licence has a baton endorsement` `the baton is a type the Commissioner approved` `my baton training is within the last 12 months`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I carry a firearm at work for this task (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 23-25; Regulations reg 9, Sch 1 cl 9(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `the task` IS AN `Armed task` @desc What you would be doing while armed
      `my licence has a firearm endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your security officer's licence is endorsed under s 24
      `I hold a permit for this occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a s 25 permit for this display or special occasion
      `the security agent provided the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the firearm was provided to you by the security agent you work for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I carry a firearm at work for this task` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I carry a firearm for this task` `the task` `my licence has a firearm endorsement` `I hold a permit for this occasion` `the security agent provided the firearm`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4A, 4B, regs 24, 25 -- am I a prohibited person`

@export Is this matter a finding of guilt under the Act (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been charged with an offence, anywhere, or been cautioned or referred for one (the questions about a past matter arise only then)
      `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this matter a finding of guilt` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is this a finding of guilt` `the matter`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many years does this matter disqualify me (Regulations reg 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been charged with an offence, anywhere, or been cautioned or referred for one (the questions about a past matter arise only then)
      `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
GIVETH A `Years of disqualification`
`For how many years does this matter disqualify me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence`
        THEN `disqualified for` (`How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `the matter`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this matter make me a prohibited person on this day (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4A; Regulations reg 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been charged with an offence, anywhere, or been cautioned or referred for one (the questions about a past matter arise only then)
      `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this matter make me a prohibited person on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I have a past charge or other matter for an offence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Am I a prohibited person because of it` `the matter` `on`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I a prohibited person on this day, taking all my past matters together (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my matters` IS A LIST OF `My past matter` @desc Every charge against you and what came of each
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a prohibited person on this day, on all my matters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a prohibited person` `my matters` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 52, 52A, 53, 57(1), regs 16, 17, Sch 4 -- can I be issued a licence`

@export Which training course must I complete for a security officer's licence (Regulations reg 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS A `My application` @desc Your application for a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Training course, if it arises`
`Which training course must I complete for a security officer's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `the answer is` (`Which training course must I complete` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May a security officer's licence be issued to me (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 52, 52A, 53)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS A `My application` @desc Your application for a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Licence decision, if it arises`
`May a security officer's licence be issued to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `the answer is` (`Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was I given written reasons for refusing my licence in time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 57(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the licensing officer refused to issue me a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensing officer has refused your application for a licence (s 57(1))
      `the date of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc The day the licensing officer decided to refuse
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the written notice with reasons
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was I given written reasons for refusing my licence in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `the licensing officer refused to issue me a licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was I given reasons for the refusal in time` `the date of the refusal` `the date of the notice`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What fee must I pay (Security and Related Activities (Control) Regulations 1997 reg 54, Sch 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Fee item` @desc What you are applying for
      `my fingerprints and palm prints are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer requires your fingerprints and palm prints for a licence or its renewal
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What fee must I pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `amount` (`What fee do I pay` `the item` `my fingerprints and palm prints are required`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 42A, 49, 55, 57(2), 60 -- how long it runs and renewing it`

@export For how long will my licence run (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 42A, 60)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a temporary licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a temporary licence for an interstate resident (s 42A)
      `it is the first issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first time the licence is issued to you
      `it is for a special event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is for the duration of a special event or events
      `I asked for a period shorter than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for less than 3 years
GIVETH A `Licence term, if it arises`
`For how long will my licence run` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `the answer is` (`How long will my licence run` `it is a temporary licence` `it is the first issue` `it is for a special event` `I asked for a period shorter than 3 years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my application to renew my licence on time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 49(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `the expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence is due to expire
      `the day the application is received` IS A DATE @desc The day the licensing officer receives your renewal application
      `the licensing officer allowed a later time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer allowed you to apply later
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my application to renew my licence on time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my renewal application on time` `the expiry date` `the day the application is received` `the licensing officer allowed a later time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my licence be renewed (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 55)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `my past matters` IS A LIST OF `My past matter` @desc Every charge against you and what came of each
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the renewal is decided
      `the ground` IS A `Ground against renewal` @desc The ground, in the licensing officer's opinion, against renewing your licence
      `the officer thinks renewing is appropriate anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer thinks it appropriate to renew despite a minor ground
GIVETH A `Renewal decision, if it arises`
`May my licence be renewed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `the answer is` (`Can my licence be renewed` `my past matters` `the date of the decision` `the ground` `the officer thinks renewing is appropriate anyway`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was I told in time that my licence would not be renewed (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 57(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the licensing officer refused to renew my licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensing officer has refused to renew your licence (s 57(2))
      `the expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence is due to expire
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given written notice of the refusal and the reasons
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was I told in time that my licence would not be renewed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `the licensing officer refused to renew my licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was I told in time that my licence will not be renewed` `the expiry date` `the date of the notice`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 61, 77, 77A, Sch 1 -- at work and afterwards`

@export May I start my shift on these facts (Regulations Sch 1 Div 2 cl 7, 9(3), 11B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `I hold a current first aid certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current first aid certificate from an approved course
      `I am wearing an approved uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are wearing a uniform of a type the Commissioner approved
      `I am doing retail loss prevention, or an escort the officer allowed out of uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the uniform exception in cl 7(3) applies to you
      `I carry a weapon other than an authorised firearm or baton` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are carrying any other weapon
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I start my shift on these facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I start my shift` `I hold a current first aid certificate` `I am wearing an approved uniform` `I am doing retail loss prevention, or an escort the officer allowed out of uniform` `I carry a weapon other than an authorised firearm or baton`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I show my identity card to this person (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 61(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `who is asking` IS A `Who is asking` @desc Who asked to see your card
      `I was issued an identity card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensing officer issued you an identity card
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I show my identity card to this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I show my identity card` `who is asking` `I was issued an identity card`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I tell the licensing officer about this, and by when (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 77(2), 77A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `the event` IS A `What happened to me` @desc What happened
GIVETH A `Notice duty, if it arises`
`Must I tell the licensing officer about this, and by when` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `the answer is` (`Must I tell the licensing officer` `the event`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did I tell the licensing officer about this in time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 77(2), 77A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `the event` IS A `What happened to me` @desc What happened
      `the date it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the charge, finding or move
      `the date I told them` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the licensing officer notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Did I tell the licensing officer about this in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Did I tell the licensing officer in time` `the event` `the date it happened` `the date I told them`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 67A, 72, 79B, 80 -- what can happen to my licence, and review`

@export What happens to my licence after the Commissioner's conclusion (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 67A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `the conclusion` IS A `What the Commissioner concludes` @desc What the Commissioner has concluded about you
GIVETH A `What happens to my licence, if it arises`
`What happens to my licence after the Commissioner's conclusion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What happens to my licence` `the conclusion`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Commissioner direct me to give a blood or urine sample (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 79B, 80)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence now
      `I hold a crowd controller's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a crowd controller's licence
      `my security officer's licence has a firearm or baton endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is endorsed under s 24 or s 26
      `I hold a firearm permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a s 25 permit with your security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Commissioner direct me to give a blood or urine sample` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I hold a security officer's licence`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Commissioner direct me to give a sample` `I hold a crowd controller's licence` `my security officer's licence has a firearm or baton endorsement` `I hold a firearm permit`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review this decision (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 72)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the decision` IS A `Licensing decision` @desc The licensing officer's decision
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review this decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN `yes if` (`May I ask the Tribunal to review this decision` `the decision`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 16, 64, 88A, Sch 5 -- penalties`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for this offence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 16, 51, 61, 64, 75, 77, 77A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a court can fine me for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most a court can fine me` `the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be given an infringement notice for this offence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 88A; Regulations Sch 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given an infringement notice for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given an infringement notice` `the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for this offence on an infringement notice (Regulations Sch 5 Div 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the modified penalty for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work, or want to work, as a security officer` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the modified penalty` `the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a business that supplies security officers to others, a security agent (ss 11, 15, 19, 20, 21, 43)`

-- s 11: "A security agent is a person who supplies the services of -- (a) security officers". s 15: such a person "must
-- not act as a security agent except under the authority of a security agent's licence"; s 43(2) lets a director or
-- officer hold it for a body corporate. s 19(1): a licensed security officer "must not act as such unless he or she does
-- so as an employee of a security agent". s 20(1)(a): "A person must not employ as a -- (a) security officer a person
-- who does not hold a security officer's licence". s 21(1): no advertising or holding out a willingness to supply
-- security officers' services "unless the person holds a security agent's licence" (held for them under s 43(2) counts,
-- s 21(2)). Each is "Penalty: a fine of $15 000"; Regulations Sch 5 Div 1 items 1, 7 and 8 set a $500 modified penalty.

§§§ `ss 11, 15, 43 -- the business's own licence`

@export Must my business hold a security agent's licence, held for a company by one of its directors or officers (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 11, 15, 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my business hold a security agent's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN `yes if` (`Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence` TRUE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my business advertise, or hold out, that it is willing to supply security officers (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a security agent's licence is held by me or on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security agent's licence, or one is held on your behalf by a director or officer (s 43(2))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my business advertise that it supplies security officers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN `yes if` `a security agent's licence is held by me or on my behalf`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19, 20 -- the officers it supplies`

@export May my business employ this person as a security officer (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 20(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person holds a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person holds a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my business employ this person as a security officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN `yes if` `the person holds a security officer's licence`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May a licensed security officer work for my business on these terms (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the officer works for me under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer is your employee under a contract of service or an apprenticeship, rather than a contractor
      `the officer holds a security agent's licence themselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer holds a security agent's licence of their own
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a licensed security officer work for my business on these terms` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN `yes if` (`As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` TRUE `the officer works for me under a contract of service or apprenticeship` TRUE `the officer holds a security agent's licence themselves`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 15, 20, 21, Sch 5 -- penalties`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for this offence of my business (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 15, 20, 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `the offence` IS A `My business's offence` @desc The offence your business is said to have committed
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a court can fine me for this offence of my business` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN amount (`the most a court can fine for` `the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty on an infringement notice for this offence of my business (Regulations Sch 5 Div 1 items 1, 7, 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `the offence` IS A `My business's offence` @desc The offence your business is said to have committed
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the modified penalty for this offence of my business` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business that supplies security officers to others` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN amount (`the modified penalty for` `the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person who hires or employs security for their own property (ss 12, 15, 16, 20)`

-- s 12(2): "A person employed by one employer only, who is not a security agent, to watch, guard or protect the property
-- of that employer is not within the definition in subsection (1) unless the person is in possession of a firearm or
-- baton". So a guard the client employs directly needs a security officer's licence only if the guard has another
-- employer or carries a firearm or baton, and only then may the client not employ the guard without one (s 20(1)(a):
-- $15 000; Sch 5 item 7: $500). A firm the client hires to supply guards is a security agent (s 11) and must be licensed
-- (s 15). This role is for a person who is not a security agent; one who is takes the second role.

§§§ `ss 12, 16, 20 -- a guard I employ myself`

@export Does a guard I employ myself to guard my own property need a security officer's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 12, 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property` @desc Whether you employ your own guard, hire a security firm to supply guards, or both
      `the guard works only for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guard is employed by you only, and by no other employer, to guard your own property
      `the guard carries a firearm or baton` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guard carries a firearm or baton while working
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a guard I employ myself need a security officer's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hire or employ security for my own property` THEN
        IF `I employ my own guard, in` `how I get security for my property`
        THEN `yes if` (`Am I a security officer` (`the work of my own guard` `the guard works only for me` `the guard carries a firearm or baton`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I employ this guard to guard my own property (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 12, 20(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property` @desc Whether you employ your own guard, hire a security firm to supply guards, or both
      `the guard works only for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guard is employed by you only, and by no other employer, to guard your own property
      `the guard carries a firearm or baton` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guard carries a firearm or baton while working
      `the guard holds a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guard holds a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I employ this guard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hire or employ security for my own property` THEN
        IF `I employ my own guard, in` `how I get security for my property`
        THEN `yes if` (`the guard holds a security officer's licence` OR (NOT `Am I a security officer` (`the work of my own guard` `the guard works only for me` `the guard carries a firearm or baton`)))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for employing as a security officer a guard who does not hold a security officer's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property` @desc Whether you employ your own guard, hire a security firm to supply guards, or both
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for employing an unlicensed guard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hire or employ security for my own property` THEN
        IF `I employ my own guard, in` `how I get security for my property`
        THEN amount (`the most a court can fine for` `employing an unlicensed person as a security officer (s 20)`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty on an infringement notice for employing an unlicensed guard (Regulations Sch 5 Div 1 item 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property` @desc Whether you employ your own guard, hire a security firm to supply guards, or both
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the modified penalty for employing an unlicensed guard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hire or employ security for my own property` THEN
        IF `I employ my own guard, in` `how I get security for my property`
        THEN amount (`the modified penalty for` `employing an unlicensed person as a security officer (s 20)`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 11, 15 -- a security firm I hire`

@export Must the security firm I hire to supply guards hold a security agent's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 11, 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I get security for my property` IS A `How I get security for my property` @desc Whether you employ your own guard, hire a security firm to supply guards, or both
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the security firm I hire hold a security agent's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hire or employ security for my own property` THEN
        IF `I hire a security firm, in` `how I get security for my property`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence` TRUE)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
